# Draft: kk: keep independent geometry shader side effects in the compute pass
# https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/merge_requests/45798 state=closed
# In this MR, I updated poly’s geometry shader emulation so that work only used for side effects (like buffer stores or atomics) stays in the compute pass instead of being replayed again during rasterization. I enabled this optimization for KosmicKrisp, while keeping the default behavior intact for existing poly callers. If a shader has texture operations or atomics that affect outputs or control flow, it safely falls back to the standard path. I also rebased this into a clean two-commit series on current upstream (poly helper first, then KK hookup) and stripped out all unrelated commits from the earlier branch. On Linux, the logic passed 36 CPU test cases with NIR validation enabled. 

My MacBook is currently in for repair, so I haven’t been able to retest this isolated rebase on native Apple hardware yet. Because of that, I’m keeping this MR as a Draft for now. All previous test runs, build logs, and validation reports on macOS / Apple silicon are available on my GitHub: https://github.com/niltonperimneto/mesa. I’d appreciate any feedback on the approach while I wait for my machine to come back!

_AI disclosure: This series was prepared with AI assistance; commits carry Generated-by: LLM._
